  "findings": "Directly inspected the with-candidate Chromium frames at 390px index 3 and 320px index 2 and verified the remaining frames through the receipt's measured bounds. With the V2b candidate, every endpoint submenu is contained inside the viewport with all items legible, identical in presentation to the pre-change Chromium rendering (the Firefox-only block is inert in Chromium and the generic block's anchoring is untouched); all 16 measured rows show off-left 0 and off-right 0 in both variants. This receipt is the route-(b) cross-engine record required by LANE-ALLOCATION-35; it is supplementary and is not the ledger-bound certification, because a Firefox-only block can demonstrate no A/B need in Chromium."
